Our project, the Robotic Assistive Luggage Handling System (RALHS), was designed to improve efficiency and accessibility in airport 
baggage claim areas by integrating RFID technology for luggage identification and UWB modules for tracking and following a specific user,
along with a robotic arm and mobile platform to automate sorting and delivery, with a key focus on accessibility to support elderly 
passengers and individuals with reduced mobility by reducing the physical effort required to retrieve luggage.
